---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="LCR Labs is an independent software label building small, native, privacy-respecting utilities for macOS."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="head">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>An independent software label</h1>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          LCR Labs builds small, carefully designed tools for Apple platforms. The focus is
          macOS: utilities that do one job properly, look and behave like the system they run
          on, and stay out of the way the rest of the time.
        </p>

        <h2>What that means in practice</h2>
        <p>
          The apps are written in Swift and SwiftUI using Apple’s own frameworks, rather than
          wrapped web interfaces. That is not a technical preference for its own sake — it is
          what makes an app feel native: the right typography, the right spacing, working
          keyboard navigation, sensible window behaviour, correct dark and light appearances,
          and a resource footprint small enough that you can leave the app running.
        </p>
        <p>
          Data stays on the device by default. A system monitor should not need an account, a
          note-taking companion should not upload your email, and a pointer utility should not
          be interested in how you use your displays. Where a product later benefits from
          synchronisation, the intent is user-controlled iCloud rather than a database owned
          by LCR Labs.
        </p>

        <h2>How the apps are distributed</h2>
        <p>
          LCR Labs applications are distributed through <span class="nowrap">Setapp</span>,
          which handles installation, licensing, payment and the associated billing support.
          This website exists to explain the products and point you to the right place — it is
          not a shop, and it does not process payments or host paid downloads.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Product questions, bug reports and feedback are welcome through the
          <a href="/support/">support page</a>. Legal contact details are listed in the
          <a href="/imprint/">imprint</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="actions">
        <Button href="/products/" variant="primary">View the products</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .head h1 {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .actions {
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
  }

  .nowrap {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
